<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuala Selangor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuala Selangor is a town at the mouth of the Selangor River on the west coast of Peninsular Malaysia. In the 18th century it was the seat of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultans</a> of Selangor, defended by a fort on Bukit Melawati overlooking the estuary. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> captured it briefly in 1784, and the royal centre later shifted towards Klang and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuala-lumpur">Kuala Lumpur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuala-selangor.jpg" alt="Kuala Selangor" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LinEnn21 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lighthouse_of_Bukit_Melawati.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
